+# AN-900: Record a consent for a person
+
+- **Jira:** AN-900
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2, 3)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:**
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: none (other modules learn through the event `identity.consent-changed`)
+
+## Context
+
+The platform records the consents of a person, for example for marketing e-mails. Head office must prove each consent (T4 privacy controls), and `identity` owns consents (architecture section 4, T3-D-009).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| T3-AC-004 | `packages/core/src/identity/consent.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** `packages/core/src/identity/AGENTS.md`
+  - `createIdentity({ repo, consents, bus, clock })`: new required dependency `consents: ConsentRepository`.
+  - `.recordConsent({ personId, purpose, textVersion, channel, granted }): Promise<ConsentRecord>`. Throws `UnknownPersonError` for an unknown person, `InvalidConsentError` for an empty purpose or text version, an unknown channel, or a decision that is not a boolean.
+  - `.currentConsent(personId, purpose): Promise<ConsentRecord | null>`: the latest record.
+  - `.consentHistory(personId): Promise<ConsentRecord[]>`: oldest first, ordered by `decidedAt`, then `id`.
+  - New exports: `InMemoryConsentRepository`, `CONSENT_CHANNELS`, `UnknownPersonError`, `InvalidConsentError`, types `ConsentRecord`, `ConsentRepository`, `ConsentChannel`, `ConsentChanged`, `RecordConsentInput`.
+  - Invariant: a consent record is never changed or deleted; a new decision adds a record (T3-AC-004).
+- **Contracts:** event `identity.consent-changed`, emitted after each `recordConsent`. Payload `consentId`, `personId`, `purpose`; no personal data. A consumer reads the decision with `currentConsent`. [ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-consent-changed-event.md).
+- **Schema:** table `identity.consent`, append-only.
+
+  | Column | Type | Personal | Category | Purpose | Owner | Retention |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+  | `id` | uuid, PK | no | | | | |
+  | `person_id` | uuid, FK `identity.person.id` | no | | | | |
+  | `purpose` | text | no | | | | |
+  | `text_version` | text | no | | | | |
+  | `channel` | text: `web`, `advisor`, `import` | yes | preference | Prove each consent decision of the person | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+  | `granted` | boolean | yes | preference | same | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+  | `decided_at` | timestamptz | yes | preference | same | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+
+  Index `(person_id, purpose, decided_at)` for the current read. The category `preference` exists; no new category.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- The AC text maps onto fields: "type" → `purpose`, "text version" → `textVersion`, "date" → `decidedAt`, "source" → `channel`, "withdrawal" → a record with `granted: false`. This is a mapping, not a contradiction of T3-AC-004.
+- `purpose` is a free, trimmed string, not an enum: the purposes are not listed in the story; head office adds them without a code change.
+- The time of the decision is the clock time of the call. The story does not ask for a back-dated time (an import with old times is the migration, out of scope).
+- `channel`, `granted` and `decided_at` are personal data (consent choices, data conventions); the person ID, purpose and text version are references, like `journey.task.person_id`.
+- The in-memory store freezes each record, so a caller cannot change a stored record.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- The consent screens.
+- The e-mail marketing tool interface.
+- The migration of old consents.
+- The Drizzle repository and the migration of `identity.consent` (the fixture uses in-memory stores, like `identity.person`).
+
+## Open questions
+
+None.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
